    h3 Improved thread navigation in W3C's mailing list archives @17,1348,82,112
    text A new feature is available in W3C's mailing list archives, aiming to make it easier to read and navigate message threads. @17,1472,82,264
    text Blog @17,1748,82,21
  col @111,1385,141,346
    h3 Introducing group activity pages @111,1385,141,38
    text W3C groups now have an Activity page that shows, month by month, their charters, publications, meetings, participants and GitHub work in one place. The pages are in beta, and we would like your feedback. @111,1435,141,264
    text Blog @111,1711,141,20
  col @264,1415,344,286
    h3 We’re on a roll - EPUB 3.4 is coming @264,1415,344,19
    text The Publishing Maintenance Working Group at W3C has been quietly working on yet another update for the EPUB3 standard, and we're excited to share what we have been up to. Our goal is to not only maintain the EPUB standard, but do our best to keep it in line with the needs of industry, and this update does exactly that. Your existing books do not need to change, if they conform to previous EPUB versions, they will conform to EPUB 3.4. Content you create today will automatically conform as well. @264,1446,344,223
    text Blog @264,1681,344,20
  col @620,1367,91,382
    h3 What’s new in the W3C Website Design System @620,1367,91,94
    text A significant update to the W3C Website Design System was published at the end of September 2026. Here’s what changed and why. @620,1473,91,244
    text Blog @620,1729,91,20
